{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:afd099a7bff080077f4e1061f92493dccdd3ad79","text":"Retire this review request. It named head a86f35e1, which cannot merge. The replacement is f05049d677f854312117cb0fa9ddca56fc833f2a, naming the re-cut head 183ebe7d.\n\nTwo defects made the old head unmergeable, both fallout from the f6c96085 retirement I asked for: its limits.md still cited that retired artifact, which is a fatal class in the citation gate, and once the citation repair merged it conflicted with main in that same file. Its docs artifact was stale as well. Assert b0413456 records the whole diagnosis.\n\nI held this request open deliberately after filing that assert, rather than retiring it immediately, so the back-pressure work stayed visible as an outstanding ask while it was being re-cut. Now that the replacement exists the visibility is carried by that instead, and leaving this one live would put two open review requests on the board for one piece of work, one of them pointing at a head nobody should look at.\n\nNo promise ever attached to this request, so nothing in flight is cancelled by retiring it. That mattered enough to check: retiring a request a reviewer has already promised against cancels the commitment underneath them and leaves any verdict bound to nothing."}